				\begin{document}$$\frac{1}{\sqrt{X}}$$\end{document}1X. Thus, in principle, increasing the DNA input amount or the number of genomic sites to quantify in the same gene would improve the limit of detection (LoD). Because the DNA input is usually limited especially in plasma-derived cfDNA, to overcome the Poisson distribution problem, ensemble of quantitation modules to sample a large number of independent genomic loci on the same gene is required to further improve CNV sensitivity. Highly multiplexed ddPCR remains challenging due to limited fluorescence channels.

